          "distinct": true,
          "id": "10f8830feafef0034a88759a6b30663527851f03",
          "message": "Give f64 log2 a native base-2 fast leg\n\nlog2 computed ln_fast_raw(x) × log2(e) — a closing double-double multiply\n(plus ln's e·LN2_LO fold) on the gate path, paying a conversion tax where\nCORE-MATH's dedicated log2 exploits base 2: the exponent join is exact.\n\nNew LOG2_CELLS table (same exact-z reciprocal lattice as LN_CELLS, l words\nin base 2 on the 2^-42 grid so e + l1 is exact as a plain add), generated\nby tools/gen_log2_exact_f64.py, which re-verifies the per-cell Fast2Sum\norderings against max|zh| = max|z|·LOG2_E_HI·(1+2^-53) — the leg's linear\nterm z·log2(e) is no longer exact, so it carries its FMA residual and the\nz·LOG2_E_LO sliver in the low word, and the base-e tail polynomial is\nreused scaled by LOG2_E_HI on the way in.  Error budget stays the base-e\nleg's <2^-66 scaled by log2(e) plus ~2^-67 of new low-word rounding;\nLOG2_ZIV_EPS and the dint::log2_accurate fallback are unchanged.\n\nln_exact_reduce is parameterized over the cell table (exact_reduce_in);\nthe base-e callers are untouched (log same-run ratio 0.994, unchanged).\n\nmetallic::log2 15.56 → 15.19 ns (−2.2%, p = 0.00 on a calm box), same-run\nCORE-MATH ratio 1.07 → 1.05.  Verified: log2 dense + bit sweeps and the\nworst-case corpus bit-exact, plus a new test_log2_vs_mpfr independent\n2M-point sweep (log2.rs previously had no MPFR gate).\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_0146rStmW9uuSqfNurfTQWYd",
          "timestamp": "2026-07-02T13:14:36+08:00",
          "tree_id": "688e2a5a14a8a9397a310c78ec2902abada3aa37",
          "url": "https://github.com/jdh8/metallic-rs/commit/10f8830feafef0034a88759a6b30663527851f03"
