          "distinct": true,
          "id": "99f740b5a85961620ebd282f2f91a6f9ebc56b71",
          "message": "Certify the log-family Ziv gates with MPFR soundness proofs\n\nThe recent fast legs (log2's native base-2 leg, log1p's [2⁻⁸, 2⁻⁴)\npolynomial leg) shipped with prose-only error budgets — log.rs was the\nonly kernel file with no ziv_soundness module.  Extract the gated legs\n(log2_fast_raw, log1p_small_eval, log1p_wide_eval, log1p_table_raw) and\nprove all six gates sound vs 250-bit MPFR: worst |err|/gate = ln 0.080,\nlog2 0.068, log10 0.036, log1p small 0.069, wide 0.222, table 0.093.\nAdd the previously-uncommitted 2.1M-point wide-band sweep vs core-math\nto default tests, and test_log1p_vs_mpfr / test_log10_vs_mpfr — every\nlog-family fn now has the independent MPFR gate.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>",
          "timestamp": "2026-07-03T06:56:42+08:00",
          "tree_id": "e274d862084745ec22250299da8385788f2c8adc",
