          "distinct": true,
          "id": "e0b3ced3f3c814f195744e8df700e69a38d14c36",
          "message": "Silence the deliberate suboptimal_flops sites so clippy is green on main\n\nFive raw multiply-add shapes are intentional, not missed FMAs: cbrt's\nHalley/Newton products and lgamma's digamma correction overlap in the\nOoO window and their exact roundings are what the certified error\nbudgets assume, and the two test-module sites mirror analytic bounds\nor generate test inputs. Targeted allows with the reasons keep the\ncrate-level deny meaningful and stop future sessions from\nmisattributing a red  to their own changes.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>",
          "timestamp": "2026-07-03T20:12:26+08:00",
          "tree_id": "b3c7ebfae32d63687445bc1d0a7594a1efc723c0",
