          "distinct": true,
          "id": "e7fe56846c6c9f3a91c80587e41222062071bd5f",
          "message": "Correct the bench playbook: concurrent runs corrupt pair ratios\n\nAn 8-way concurrent f32 sweep on the 8-physical-core box inflated\nabsolute times up to 2× and skewed within-pair ratios in both\ndirections (atanhf 1.75 vs true 1.02, expm1f 0.64 vs true 1.06):\nhyperthread-sibling port contention hits a table-heavy arm and a\npoly-heavy arm differently.  Benches run strictly serially now.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>",
          "timestamp": "2026-07-11T20:18:28+08:00",
          "tree_id": "0e3ce386eb55c882b86f9f3088a09041eac2edb2",
