          "distinct": true,
          "id": "a23a0701feb47db062fde50ee4813611a050b643",
          "message": "Add correctly-rounded f64 compound = (1+x)^y\n\nFills the last C23 gap: compound existed only as f32 compoundf.  CORE-MATH\nships no binary64 compound, so — like tgamma/lgamma — it is MPFR-verified\nagainst a home-grown hard-to-round corpus.\n\nThe fast leg mirrors pow_fast with a 1+x front end (ln_dd_fast on the exact\n1+x double-double).  The accurate leg reuses pow's Dint/Qint cascade and\nexact/midpoint detector; since log_2/log_3 need an f64-precision base, it\nsplits ln(1+x) = ln(s.high) + ln1p(s.low/s.high) with a Newton-reciprocal\ncorrection.\n\nVerified: 30M bit-exact vs pow on the exact-1+x domain, 8M vs MPFR on the\nsmall-|x| region, a 2925-case frozen corpus, and the fast-leg Ziv soundness\n(worst |err|/slack = 0.3048, a 3.3x margin).\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.8 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>",
          "timestamp": "2026-07-11T22:32:09+08:00",
          "tree_id": "6550b5802ad4f412b9e70f62775b4da15cc656fc",
          "url": "https://github.com/jdh8/metallic-rs/commit/a23a0701feb47db062fde50ee4813611a050b643"
