          "distinct": true,
          "id": "aa55da79461e699550c563c8c3d8bdb5ea974300",
          "message": "Implement log1pq on logq's engine with an exact 256-bit 1 + x\n\nCORE-MATH has no binary128 log1p, so log1pq follows the no-upstream recipe:\nMPFR oracle, a home-grown corpus carrying its answers, oracle switch later.\n\n- `log<B>` splits into a front end and `finish::<B>(e, j, d, floor)` — the\n  fast leg, its gate and the rounder, shared unchanged.  `accurate` now takes\n  `z` at 2^333 in three limbs for every base — for logq that is its exact\n  2^-205 pair one limb up, no computation (widening it eagerly to a shifted\n  third limb kept four more registers live across the fast leg and cost\n  41 -> 54 ns) — and `log1p_wide` takes the normalized `|z|` plus `z·2^273`,\n  returning `|log(1+z)|` at the caller's scale.\n- Above `|x| = 2^-18`, `one_plus` forms `1 + x` *exactly* as a 256-bit\n  significand (`113 - e` bits below 1, `max(113, e + 1)` above): only\n  `x >= 2^256` drops its 1, a relative slip under 2^-256 inside the accurate\n  leg's own 2^-251.  Two wmuls against the 93-bit reciprocal give `z` exact\n  at 2^-348; the frame keeps 2^-333 of it, fifteen bits under its own\n  2^-342 and nothing against a result of 2^-19 or more.  ziv_soundness\n  worst |err|/gate 0.1166 (8.6x), logq's number.\n- Below 2^-18 the argument is its own reduced `z`: `ratio` (the fast leg's\n  polynomial with its final multiply split off) times the input significand\n  in floating form, full relative accuracy down to 2^-113, its own gate on\n  the 128-bit discarded field (SMALL_GATE = 2^118; worst |err|/gate 0.2237,\n  4.5x) and `small_accurate` via `log1p_wide` at 256 bits.  Below 2^-113\n  the answer is x; at ±2^-112 the square is exactly half an ulp and the\n  cube breaks the tie — both asserted in-source.\n- Gates: tests/cases/log1pq.wc (69,913 cases) from\n  examples/gen_f128_log_cases.rs -- 1p (seams ±2^-113/-112/-18, `2^±k - 1`,\n  powers of two both signs with every position of the 1 through 2^256,\n  round(e^z - 1) for 114-bit midpoints down to result binade 2^-113, MPFR\n  scans of the domain, of -1 + 2^-113..2^-1 and of the floating band),\n  CORE-MATH's f64 log1p as the oracle-free cross-check, MPFR sweeps.\n- Fixes the `positive` samplers of tests/all/f128_/log{,2,10}q.rs, whose\n  `bits >> 120 % 0x7fff` left 8 bits and so only ever drew exponent fields\n  0..255; they now cover every binade.\n- Bench baseline is GCC libquadmath until upstream binds cr_log1pq:\n  62.3 ns vs 1226 ns (20x).  logq A/B'd old vs new back to back: 54.4 ns\n  both (core_math 44-52 ns in the same windows, box at load ~40).\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5.1 <noreply@anthropic.com>",
