          "distinct": true,
          "id": "a87dd5da9084a7cb3c4ffa714a24fb031d29b8f6",
          "message": "perf(f128): inline hypotq's root helpers, which sat behind GOT-indirect calls\n\nProbing each parity-bound entry point from its own binary (an\n#[inline(never)] wrapper calling through a black_box'd fn pointer, then\nobjdump -dr) showed hypotq's fast path reaching hypot::hypot_fixed and, once\nthat was inlined, roots::sqrt_wide through GOT-indirect calls: neither had an\ninline hint, and the #[inline] entry point is instantiated in the caller's\ncrate, so every draw paid a cross-crate call plus the spills around it.\n#[inline(always)] on both (each has two callers); zero numerical change, so\nno Ziv re-certification.  sqrt_fixed/rsqrt_fixed/cbrt_fixed are the same\nshape behind sqrtq/rsqrtq/cbrtq and get #[inline].\n\nInterleaved A/B, the two binaries alternated three rounds (loaded box):\n  hypotq  A (HEAD) 73.0 / 72.5 / 73.0 ns   B 69.3 / 69.6 / 69.7 ns   (-4.7%)\n  same-run vs core_math::hypotq: 70.1 vs 72.4 ns, 0.97x (was 1.02x)\n  sqrtq   A (HEAD) 39.3 / 39.6 / 38.7 ns   B 37.8 / 38.0 / 32.5 ns   (-4%)\n\nThe same probe found atan2::atan_frac out of line at its two call sites in\natanq; #[inline(always)] there measured 68.4 vs 67.8 ns -- slower -- and is\nreverted (recorded in the skill's dead-end table).  atan2q and logq showed\nno outlined hot helpers and no coin-flip branches.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5.1 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01Gz3yMzDVuuY7GkH9N5LFki",
          "timestamp": "2026-09-05T18:14:49+08:00",
          "tree_id": "adc02d747dd46040903f69948d0a2f65850813cb",
