          "distinct": true,
          "id": "d0a33724bae3dbf5d0ee780936aff4d9146ecd37",
          "message": "fix(f128): correct root_256's leading-zero bound to 112\n\n`1 − x²` bottoms out at `2^-112·(1 − 2^-114)` for `x = 1 − 2^-113`, which\nsits just under `2^-112` and has 112 leading zeros in the 256-bit frame,\nnot 111.  The debug assertion fired on `known_values` in CI's\ndebug-assertions build only; release builds (where it was tested) skip\nit.  The code already handled the shift (`parity = 112`), so nothing\nelse changes.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5.1 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_018mbguBhZzLKTkzq8ia4JLY",
          "timestamp": "2026-09-05T18:56:03+08:00",
          "tree_id": "c295e8989f1dd1352634ad87176bb78b11a95729",
          "url": "https://github.com/jdh8/metallic-rs/commit/d0a33724bae3dbf5d0ee780936aff4d9146ecd37"
